@startuml
title AsyncSharedState<T> — task completion state machine

[*] --> Pending : create shared state

Pending --> Suspended : waiter successfully registered
Pending --> Signaled : producer publishes completion before waiter registration
Suspended --> Signaled : producer publishes completion

Signaled --> [*] : future consumes result and releases ownership
Pending --> [*] : endpoints abandoned / last reference released
Suspended --> [*] : waiter and producer release final references

note right of Pending
  Shared state is created dynamically by makeAsyncState<T>(allocator).
  The factory returns move-only AsyncPromise<T> and AsyncFuture<T>
  endpoints that share ownership of the state.
end note

note right of Suspended
  The waiter handle and selected executor are published before the
  Pending -> Suspended transition. If completion wins the race, the
  awaiter does not remain suspended.
end note

note right of Signaled
  Cancellation is a separate cooperative flag; it is not a completion
  state. Dropping a promise without publishing a value completes the
  state as cancelled.
end note
@enduml
